# StableSense frontend environment
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in as needed. Do not commit .env.
#
# Where live data comes from: the dashboard reads the optional same-origin
# backend (backend/), which persists market snapshots from its Helix fetch
# cron into SQLite and serves them at /api/market. No keys are needed in the
# frontend for the core dashboard. Coin-tab price charts and exchange tickers
# still load browser-direct from CoinGecko (keyless, CORS-open).
#
# This file only configures the optional AI/backend pointer.

# Optional: point the frontend at your AI/backend service (the lite VPS in
# backend/). Empty default means same-origin (nginx serves /api/* next to the
# static app) and the AI layer is disabled when no backend is present.
# Runtime window.STABLESENSE_CONFIG.aiApiBase wins over this build-time value.
#   STABLESENSE_AI_API_BASE=https://your-backend.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI is generated only by Helix. StableSense reads stored per-coin commentary.
# HELIX_API_KEY stays in backend/.env, never in this frontend configuration.
# See backend/.env.example. No model-provider key is needed by StableSense.
